# Scope: local, ad-hoc `semgrep` runs inside THIS repository only.
#
# This file does NOT affect CI scans of your project. The reusable workflow
# checks this repo out to `.semgrep-rules/`, while semgrep reads
# `.semgrepignore` from the scan root — so this file is never consulted there.
# CI exclusions live in the `--exclude` flags in
# `.github/workflows/semgrep.yml`; change them there, not here.
#
# Three paths are deliberately NOT excluded in CI even though they appear
# below, because each is a plausible place for a real credential to land:
#   prisma/migrations/  seeded SQL can carry connection strings
#   public/static/      committed .env files and keys end up here
#   **/*.d.ts           cheap to scan, no reason to carve out

node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
.next/
.turbo/
generated/
prisma/migrations/
**/*.min.js
**/*.map
**/*.d.ts
.git/
.cache/
tmp/
temp/
logs/
*.log
vendor/
public/static/
.nuxt/
out/
.output/
storybook-static/
